/*!
@defgroup etmr
@ingroup mod_timer eTMR (Enhanced Timer)
@details
@brief eTMR Peripheral Driver.

## Overview

The eTMR (Enhanced Timer) module is a versatile timer/counter peripheral
supporting multiple operating modes: PWM, Input Capture, Output Compare,
Timer/Counter, and Quadrature Decoder.

## Hardware Features

- Configurable clock source (internal, external, or IPC clock)
- Prescaler: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128
- 16-bit counter with up-counting and center-aligned modes
- Up to 8 independent channels per instance
- PWM mode with complementary outputs, dead-time insertion, and fault protection
- Input Capture mode with edge detection, pulse-width and period measurement
- Output Compare mode with set, clear, or toggle on match
- Quadrature Decoder mode with input filtering and direction detection
- Register synchronization with software/hardware triggers
- Global time-base support for multi-instance synchronization
- Up to 4 fault inputs for global fault control

## Sub-modules

| Sub-module | Group | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Common | @ref etmr_common | Initialization, counter control, sync, interrupt, and status |
| PWM | @ref etmr_pwm_driver | PWM channel initialization, duty-cycle and period updates |
| IC | @ref etmr_ic_driver | Input capture with edge detection and measurement |
| OC | @ref etmr_oc_driver | Output compare channel configuration and match updates |
| MC | @ref etmr_mc_driver | Timer/counter mode with start/stop and period control |
| QD | @ref etmr_qd_driver | Quadrature decoder mode with direction and position |

## Integration Guide

### Compilation Units

The following files need to be compiled in the project:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_common.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_hw_access.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_pwm_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_ic_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_oc_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_mc_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/etmr_qd_driver.c
@endverbatim

### Include Paths

@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/etmr/
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/etmr/
@endverbatim

### Dependencies

- @ref clock_manager — Required for enabling the eTMR peripheral clock.
- @ref interrupt_manager — Required for channel and fault interrupt handling.

*/
